5.1: Abdominal
Wall, Inguinal Area & Scrotum
Anterior Abdominal
Wall
Nine regions
delineated by 
midclavicular lines (
reach midinguinal point)
and 
intertubercular plane
(across iliac crest
tubercles) and 
transpyloric plane
(between jugular notch
and top of pubic symphysis)
-
hypochondrial
and 
epigastric
regions superior
-
umbilical
and 
lumbar
regions middle
-
hypogastric
and 
iliac
areas inferiorly.
Abdominal Muscles &
Incisions
(231-4)
Separate in flanks, 
fused
ventrally into the rectus
.

