I use Lord’s procedure when the hydorcele is small or medium-sized and the wall of the hydrocele is thin. Otherwise the placation leaves an excessive mass. Jaboulay is preferable for thick-walled sacs or large hydrocele.
However the dissection to create the pocket
for the hydrocele increases the risk of haematoma formation.
