varicocele
Dilatation and tortuosity of pampiniform
plexus of veins.

as for inguinal hernia. Open external oblique aponeurosis, mobilize the cord and split the cremasteric fascia longitudinally. Separate the veins from the vas and testiclar artery and ligate all enlarged veins with 2/0 Vicryl ties.
Repair the external oblique aponeurosis
Complications:
o
Early: bleeding,
infection, the veins in the scrotum become hard until the
thrombosis organised, acute hydrocele, damage to the
ilio-inguinal nerve. 
o
Late recurrenc due to
recanlization of veins
